# --- Player_task13.events ---
# Task 13: Footstep sounds by material — complete, playable example
#
# Part A: `me is moving`          — true while a move/goto/face is active
# Part B: `when me touches <mat>` — fires on enter-edge contact with a material
# Part C: `play step sound "<mat>"` — plays the mapped clip, cooldown-gated (0.3s)
#
# ========================================================================
# SETUP — do these steps in the editor:
#
#  1. Create a Physical Material: Content → right-click → New → Physics →
#     Physical Material. Name it "Grass", set Tag = "Grass".
#
#  2. Floor: select the floor actor → Collider component → Material = Grass.
#     (The floor needs a Collider so contact can be detected.)
#
#  3. Player collider: select the player actor → add a Collider component
#     (Box Collider or Capsule Collider around the player). The player needs
#     a Collider so the EventSheet can detect when it touches the floor.
#
#  4. Import a step-sound clip into Content (e.g. "footstep.wav"). Clips are
#     referenced by name only — folder, extension, and case are ignored.
#
#  5. Player → EventSheet component → Step Sound Map → add entry:
#     Material = "Grass", Clip = "footstep".
#     (Add more for other surfaces: Stone → stone_step, Wood → wood_step, …)
#
#  6. Player → EventSheet component → Event File = Player_task13.
#     (Blank = the actor's own name also works.)
#
# ========================================================================
# Move with WASD so `me is moving` becomes true while walking.
when W is held
  move forward speed 5

when S is held
  move backward speed 5

when A is held
  move left speed 5

when D is held
  move right speed 5

# Walk on Grass → play the grass step sound (only while moving).
# Standing still → silence (`me is moving` is false).
# Switching floors mid-stride switches the sound on re-entry (enter-edge).

when me touches Grass and me is moving
  play step sound "Grass"

# Example additions for more surfaces — uncomment and edit to taste:
#   when me touches Stone and me is moving
#     play step sound "Stone"
#
#   when me touches Wood and me is moving
#     play step sound "Wood"
